[38;5;231m⏺[39m Understood — holding here. Nothing written; the repo is untouched.

  The design is captured in my message above if you want to reread it. Two things worth flagging while you think, since
  they're the parts most likely to change your mind:

  - [1m[38;5;153m--force[39m vs. cron.[0m You picked refuse-unless-[38;5;153m--force[39m, which means a nightly retry for a day that already exported will
    exit non-zero. That's the safe choice, but it does mean the cron line probably wants [38;5;153m--force[39m on it permanently — at
    which point the guard only protects manual invocations. Still defensible; just worth knowing where the protection
    actually lands.
  - [1mThe file shape is the contract.[0m Once something downstream parses [38;5;153mtotal_cents[39m or the CSV header, changing either is a
    breaking change. Cheap to widen later (adding fields is additive), expensive to rename or restructure.

  Ping me when you've decided and I'll implement it, or tell me what to change and I'll revise.

